findings:
- finding_id: I1
  title: Dependencies inline instead of workspace level
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Dev added chrono, uuid, tower as inline dependencies in Cargo.toml. Reviewer
    flagged unused deps but never mentioned workspace = true convention. The 6 inline
    deps were not caught.
- finding_id: I2
  title: 'FieldErrorCode missing #[non_exhaustive]'
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer LOW finding: '#[non_exhaustive] missing on public enums \u2014\
    \ lib.rs:271-276' mentions public structs without #[non_exhaustive]. However,\
    \ this flags structs not FieldErrorCode specifically. Partially caught but the\
    \ principle was flagged."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Hardcoded trace_id 'none'
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: ResponseMeta with hardcoded trace_id 'none' was not flagged by any phase.
    Reviewer noted no tracing instrumentation but did not specifically call out the
    hardcoded 'none' string in ResponseMeta.
- finding_id: I4
  title: Zero structured logging
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer HIGH finding: 'No structured logging / tracing anywhere \u2014\
    \ lib.rs (entire file)' \u2014 explicitly states 'zero tracing instrumentation\
    \ in the server \u2014 no #[instrument], no tracing::info!(), no span creation.'"
- finding_id: I5
  title: Security comment claims tracing that doesn't exist
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged the misleading SECURITY comment claiming errors are 'logged
    for debugging' when no logging exists. Reviewer noted absence of logging but did
    not identify the false documentation claim.
- finding_id: I6
  title: Non-ASCII tenant header silently treated as missing
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: TEA wrote no test for non-ASCII characters in X-Tenant-ID header. Security
    tests cover malformed JSON, large payloads, path traversal, XSS, but not non-ASCII
    header values.
- finding_id: I7
  title: "CWE-209 test gap \u2014 no body assertion"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: TEA wrote a CWE-209 test in security.rs but the pipeline output does not
    indicate body content assertions. The finding specifically notes the test checks
    status code but not response body content.
- finding_id: I8
  title: CORS preflight test doesn't verify CORS headers
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No CORS preflight test appears in the TEA test list. CORS is not mentioned
    in any test file. The CORS issue was not tested for at all.
- finding_id: I9
  title: "Wrong log levels \u2014 error! for 4xx client errors"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: "Since I4 (no logging at all) was caught by reviewer, I9 (wrong log levels\
    \ after adding logging) could not have been caught \u2014 logging was never implemented.\
    \ No phase addressed the warn! vs error! distinction."
- finding_id: I10
  title: CORS allows Any origin/method/header (CWE-942)
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged CORS configuration. TEA wrote no CORS tests, Dev presumably
    used permissive CORS defaults, and Reviewer did not mention CORS middleware configuration
    (CWE-942) in findings.
